For data x₁..xₙ: the mean x̄ = (Σxᵢ)/n; the median is the middle value when sorted; the variance s² = Σ(xᵢ−x̄)²/(n−1) (sample) and standard deviation s = √s². Worked example (verified): response times [12, 15, 13, 90, 14] ms. Mean = (12+15+13+90+14)/5 = 144/5 = 28.8. Median: sorted [12,13,14,15,90] → 14. The single outlier (90) drags the mean to 28.8 while the median stays 14 — this is why latency is reported with medians/percentiles, not means. Deviations from mean: [−16.8, −13.8, −15.8, 61.2, −14.8]; squared sum = 282.24+190.44+249.64+3745.44+219.04 = 4686.8; sample variance = 4686.8/4 = 1171.7; s ≈ 34.2 ms. Report center AND spread together — a mean without spread is a half-truth.

